    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0473" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/84</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hale to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-13T17:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In accordance with Department’s February 9, 3 p.m., I met General Tinoco at Mr.
                    Keith’s residence yesterday. Besides Mr. Keith,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d381-f1"/>
                    Tinoco’s Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs Lara, and clerk Smith <pb
                        facs="0474" n="308" xml:id="pg308"/> were present. I handed to General
                    Tinoco the copy of the note to the four other republics and read to him the part
                    addressed to him personally. He asked if it was meant to withhold recognition
                    from him even if he should be elected by a free vote.</p>
                <p>He remarked that the judicial branch of the Government which was unaffected by
                    deposition of the executive was preserving the continuity of Government.</p>
                <p>Department’s February 8, 5 p.m. Besides my own investigations I expect to get
                    written opinions from the seven ex-Presidents.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hale</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d381-f1" n="3" xml:id="d381-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. John M. Keith, an American banker in San José.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
